0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252FGyTS_V-or1j3iOgI0DFoZ7jRj1CZGavbJexL7A81VEc.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FGyTS_V-or1j3iOgI0DFoZ7jRj1CZGavbJexL7A81VEc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FGyTS_V-or1j3iOgI0DFoZ7jRj1CZGavbJexL7A81VEc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["I and III","I and II","II and IV","III and IV"],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2023","_marksId":"67fdff6d378e1624ea7b6b5c"},{"id":24033,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which one of the following molecules is chiral?","options":["<img style=\"width: 150px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png\">","<img style=\"width: 150px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-621dba7ed9c9cf92.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-621dba7ed9c9cf92.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-621dba7ed9c9cf92.png\">","<img style=\"width: 150px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-09beb7aaf9de38d5.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-09beb7aaf9de38d5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-09beb7aaf9de38d5.png\">","<img style=\"width: 150px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-fb8ab19f28e965b6.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-fb8ab19f28e965b6.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-fb8ab19f28e965b6.png\">"],"answer":0,"solution":"A molecule is chiral if it lacks a plane of symmetry (POS) and a center of symmetry (COS).<br><br>Let us analyze the given structures, which are 1,3-dioxane derivatives.<br><br>Option (1): The substituents on the ring are arranged such that there is no plane of symmetry passing through the molecule. Specifically, the methyl groups at positions 4 and 6 are trans to each other (one is wedge, the other is dash relative to the general ring plane if drawn flat). There is no POS and no COS. Thus, the molecule is chiral.<br><br>option (2): The molecule has a vertical plane of symmetry passing through the $C_2$ (acetal carbon) and $C_5$ (carbon opposite to acetal carbon). The methyl groups at $C_4$ and $C_6$ are both on wedges (cis). Thus, it has a POS and is achiral.<br><br>Option (3): Similar to option (2), the methyl groups at $C_4$ and $C_6$ are both on dashes (cis). The molecule possesses a plane of symmetry passing through $C_2$ and $C_5$. Thus, it is achiral.<br><br>Option (4): This structure also has the methyl groups at $C_4$ and $C_6$ on dashes (cis). It possesses a plane of symmetry passing through $C_2$ and $C_5$. Thus, it is achiral.<br><br>Answer : <img style=\"width: 150px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-76e2468376a924d1.png\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2026","_marksId":"6a4521838c20d3b91d64f966","answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect"},{"id":24034,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which of the following molecules are aromatic?<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252FEcgEVyLPbG9oFGcCdhgVnV44K06Ur-p778nNyZZcShM.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FEcgEVyLPbG9oFGcCdhgVnV44K06Ur-p778nNyZZcShM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FEcgEVyLPbG9oFGcCdhgVnV44K06Ur-p778nNyZZcShM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["$\\mathbf{M}, \\mathbf{N}, \\mathbf{O}$, and $\\mathbf{P}$","$\\mathbf{M}$ and $\\mathbf{O}$ only","$\\mathbf{M}, \\mathbf{N}$ and $\\mathbf{O}$ only","$\\mathbf{N}$ and $\\mathbf{P}$ only"],"answer":2,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2022","_marksId":"67fdff68378e1624ea7b6b18"},{"id":24035,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Consider the following silica-gel based thin-layer chromatogram of compounds <strong>A</strong> and <strong>B</strong>. Which one of the following statements is correct?<br>","options":["<strong>A</strong> is more polar than <strong>B</strong>; <strong>B</strong> has $R_f = 0.33$.","<strong>B</strong> is more polar than <strong>A</strong>; <strong>A</strong> has $R_f = 0.75$.","<strong>B</strong> is less polar than <strong>A</strong>; <strong>B</strong> has $R_f = 0.75$.","<strong>B</strong> is more polar than <strong>A</strong>; <strong>A</strong> has $R_f = 0.25$."],"answer":1,"solution":"The retardation factor ($R_f$) is given by the ratio of the distance travelled by the substance to the distance travelled by the solvent front.<br><br>$R_f(\\text{A}) = \\dfrac{3.75}{5} = 0.75$<br><br>$R_f(\\text{B}) = \\dfrac{1.25}{5} = 0.25$<br><br>Silica gel acts as a polar stationary phase. A more polar compound interacts more strongly with the silica gel and therefore travels a shorter distance up the plate.<br><br>Since compound B travels a shorter distance ($1.25\\text{ cm}$) compared to compound A ($3.75\\text{ cm}$), compound B is more polar than compound A.<br><br>Answer: <strong>B</strong> is more polar than <strong>A</strong>; <strong>A</strong> has $R_f = 0.75$.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2026","_marksId":"6a4521838c20d3b91d64f967"},{"id":24036,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which amongst the following are chiral compounds?<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252FMl67yqsFBsz_Fd03qoeeCWFFIIV41D2D3X_H5sUVWkw.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FMl67yqsFBsz_Fd03qoeeCWFFIIV41D2D3X_H5sUVWkw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FMl67yqsFBsz_Fd03qoeeCWFFIIV41D2D3X_H5sUVWkw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["I and II","II and IV","I and IV","II and III"],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2023","_marksId":"67fdff6d378e1624ea7b6b5a"},{"id":24037,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"General Organic Chemistry","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which one among the following compou